            <div xml:id="d38-a13">

                <pb facs="0070" n="63" xml:id="pg63"/>

                <head>L.</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Resolutions drawn up by American
                        citizens at a meeting called by Mr. J. Weinberger.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">resolutions.</hi></p>
                <p>Whereas Commissioner Carlos A. Lacayo has; against our wishes and the wishes of
                    our consul, S. C. Braida, appointed two Americans to represent us in the
                    proposed provisional government:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That it he the sentiment of this meeting
                    that any American taking part in the Lacayo government be immediately repudiated
                    by the Americans living in the reserve;</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That any so-called American that accepts
                    such a position he denounced as a renegade;</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That these resolutions be ordered printed
                    in the Bluefields Messenger.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
